### Open Questions

1. **`.users/` in this repository.** Here the tasks directory is tracked inside the code repo, so `tasks/.users/` will show up as untracked. Should this repo gitignore it, or commit the per-user pointers?
2. **Dirty foreign branch on start.** If HEAD is on a user branch other than the chosen base and has uncommitted changes, `start_task` refuses. Is that acceptable, or should those changes be carried into the new task?
3. **Re-completion after a push.** Re-completing a reopened task moves its existing final branch to the new squash commit. If that branch was already pushed, the PR needs a force-push. Is that acceptable, or should re-completion create a new suffixed final branch (e.g. `<user>/<name>-2`)?
